   $q$Read the sentence: "Mei's favorite hobby is sketching birds in the park." How does the gerund phrase "sketching birds in the park" function?$q$, $q$[{"text":"as a predicate noun that renames \"hobby\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"as the subject of the sentence","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gerund-function-subject-confusion"},{"text":"as an adjective that describes \"hobby\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gerund-participle-confusion"},{"text":"as the direct object of \"is\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"linking-verb-object-confusion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$as a predicate noun that renames "hobby"$q$, $q$The gerund phrase follows the linking verb "is" and renames the subject "hobby," so it is a predicate noun. It is not a direct object, because "is" is a linking verb and does not take an object.$q$, 'draft', null)
