   $q$Which sentence is written in the passive voice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The engineers were proud of the new bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"be-plus-adjective-as-passive"},{"text":"A team of engineers designed the bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"active-read-as-passive"},{"text":"The bridge was designed by a team of engineers.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The engineers were designing the bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"progressive-as-passive"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bridge was designed by a team of engineers.$q$, $q$In "The bridge was designed by a team of engineers," the subject receives the action and the verb is "was" plus the past participle "designed," so it is passive. "The engineers were designing the bridge" is active, because the engineers do the action.$q$, 'draft', null)
