   $q$Read the sentence: "Someone stole the bicycle from the rack last night." Which revision correctly uses the passive voice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bicycle was stolen from the rack last night.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bicycle has stole from the rack last night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-past-participle"},{"text":"The bicycle was stealing from the rack last night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"progressive-as-passive"},{"text":"The bicycle stole from the rack last night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-be-in-passive"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bicycle was stolen from the rack last night.$q$, $q$The passive voice uses a form of "be" plus the past participle, so "was stolen" is correct. "The bicycle stole" is active and wrongly makes the bicycle the thief.$q$, 'draft', null)
