   $q$Read the sentence: "It is essential that the class ____ the experiment twice to check the results." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"will repeat","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"future-for-subjunctive"},{"text":"repeats","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"indicative-for-subjunctive"},{"text":"repeat","is_correct":true},{"text":"repeated","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"past-tense-for-subjunctive"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$repeat$q$, $q$After "It is essential that," standard English uses the subjunctive base form, so "repeat" is correct. "Repeats" is the indicative form and does not belong in this kind of clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
