   $q$Read the sentence: "During the storm, the lights flickered, the dog barked, and the windows ____." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"rattle","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"},{"text":"rattled","is_correct":true},{"text":"are rattling","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"},{"text":"will rattle","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$rattled$q$, $q$The other verbs in the series, "flickered" and "barked," are past tense, so "rattled" keeps the tense consistent. "Rattle" shifts to the present tense at the end of the list.$q$, 'draft', null)
