   $q$Which sentence uses the participial phrase "Covered in mud" correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Covered in mud, the cabin was finally reached by the hikers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-participle"},{"text":"Covered in mud, reaching the cabin was a relief for the hikers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-participle"},{"text":"Covered in mud, the hikers finally reached the cabin.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Covered in mud, the cabin welcomed the tired hikers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-participle"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Covered in mud, the hikers finally reached the cabin.$q$, $q$The phrase should describe the hikers, so "the hikers" must come right after it. In the choice "Covered in mud, the cabin was finally reached by the hikers," the phrase sits next to "the cabin," so it seems the cabin is covered in mud.$q$, 'draft', null)
