   $q$Read the sentence: "Grace walked to the library to return a book about volcanoes." Which words form an infinitive?$q$, $q$[{"text":"about volcanoes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"prepositional-phrase-as-infinitive"},{"text":"to the library","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"prepositional-phrase-as-infinitive"},{"text":"to return","is_correct":true},{"text":"walked to","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"main-verb-as-infinitive"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to return$q$, $q$An infinitive is "to" followed by the base form of a verb, so "to return" is the infinitive. In "to the library," "to" is a preposition followed by a noun, not a verb.$q$, 'draft', null)
