  ('18396e7c-389f-5e42-b75a-4e3db4e57ee2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-grammar-usage'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "If the council approved the park plan, construction would begin in May, and the old fence will be removed by workers." Which revision fixes the shifts in voice and mood?$q$, $q$[{"text":"If the council approved the park plan, construction would begin in May, and workers would remove the old fence.","is_correct":true},{"text":"If the council approved the park plan, construction would begin in May, and workers removed the old fence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"},{"text":"If the council approved the park plan, construction would begin in May, and the old fence would be removed by workers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"voice-shift"},{"text":"If the council approved the park plan, construction would begin in May, and workers will remove the old fence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mood-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$If the council approved the park plan, construction would begin in May, and workers would remove the old fence.$q$, $q$The sentence describes a possible situation with the conditional "would begin," so the last clause also needs "would" and the active voice: "workers would remove the old fence." The choice "the old fence would be removed by workers" fixes the mood but keeps the passive voice.$q$, 'draft', null)
