   $q$Read the sentence: "If Nadia ____ the bus earlier, she would have arrived before the concert started." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"had caught","is_correct":true},{"text":"caught","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"simple-past-in-past-unreal"},{"text":"would have caught","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"would-in-if-clause"},{"text":"has caught","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"present-perfect-in-past-unreal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$had caught$q$, $q$For an untrue situation in the past, the "if" clause uses the past perfect "had caught" to match "would have arrived." "Would have caught" is wrong because "would" belongs in the result clause, not the "if" clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
