   $q$Which sentence uses the subjunctive mood correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The principal demanded that Sofia will join the debate team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"future-for-subjunctive"},{"text":"The principal recommended that Sofia join the debate team.","is_correct":true},{"text":"If Sofia would be on the team, the team would win more often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"would-in-if-clause"},{"text":"Sofia wishes that the debate team meets every day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"indicative-after-wish"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The principal recommended that Sofia join the debate team.$q$, $q$After "recommended that," the subjunctive uses the base form "join," as in the first sentence. "Will join" after "demanded that" uses the future tense where the subjunctive base form is needed.$q$, 'draft', null)
