   $q$Read the sentence: "Mistakes were made in the budget report by the treasurer, and the error was then corrected by her." Which revision uses the active voice consistently?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The treasurer makes mistakes in the budget report, and she then corrected the error.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"},{"text":"The treasurer made mistakes in the budget report, and the error was then corrected.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"voice-shift"},{"text":"Mistakes were made in the budget report, and the treasurer then corrected the error.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"voice-shift"},{"text":"The treasurer made mistakes in the budget report, and she then corrected the error.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The treasurer made mistakes in the budget report, and she then corrected the error.$q$, $q$Making the treasurer the subject of both clauses ("made" and "corrected") puts the whole sentence in the active voice with consistent past tense. The choice that keeps "the error was then corrected" changes only the first clause and leaves "the error was then corrected" in the passive.$q$, 'draft', null)
