   $q$Read the sentence: "Hikers following the trail map should turn left at the waterfall." What is "following the trail map"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a participial phrase that describes \"Hikers\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"the main verb of the sentence","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"participle-as-main-verb"},{"text":"a gerund phrase used as the subject","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gerund-participle-confusion"},{"text":"an infinitive phrase used as an adverb","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"verbal-type-confusion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a participial phrase that describes "Hikers"$q$, $q$The phrase describes which hikers should turn, so it is a participial phrase acting as an adjective. It is not a gerund phrase, because the subject is "Hikers," and the phrase only modifies it.$q$, 'draft', null)
