   $q$Read the sentence: "Neither the coach nor the players ____ aware that the game had been moved to Saturday." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"has been","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"agreement-with-first-subject"},{"text":"were","is_correct":true},{"text":"was","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"agreement-with-first-subject"},{"text":"is","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"agreement-with-first-subject"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$were$q$, $q$With "neither ... nor," the verb agrees with the closer subject, the plural "players," so "were" is correct. "Was" wrongly agrees with "coach," the subject farther from the verb.$q$, 'draft', null)
