   $q$Read the sentence: "When the class visited the observatory, the guide shows them a telescope that was built in 1890." Which revision fixes the error in verb tense?$q$, $q$[{"text":"When the class visited the observatory, the guide showed them a telescope that had been built in 1890.","is_correct":true},{"text":"When the class visited the observatory, the guide showed them a telescope that is built in 1890.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"present-for-past-event"},{"text":"When the class visited the observatory, the guide shows them a telescope that had been built in 1890.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"},{"text":"When the class visited the observatory, the guide will show them a telescope that was built in 1890.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tense-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When the class visited the observatory, the guide showed them a telescope that had been built in 1890.$q$, $q$The visit happened in the past, so "showed" matches "visited," and "had been built" correctly shows the building came even earlier. The choice with "the guide shows them" and "had been built" still leaves "shows" in the present tense.$q$, 'draft', null)
